  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 138 PM EDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nHeat will continue to be the big concern through the long term \nforecast. The models are in pretty good agreement that we will be at \nor just below heat advisory through next week. Daytime highs in the \nmid to upper 90s will yield apparent temperatures between 100-105 \nfor all but the highest elevations of NE Georgia. Stay hydrated and \ntake care of kids and pets. \n\nThe ridge never really breaks down, but we will return to a more \nzonal flow towards the middle of the week. This will bring back the \nchance for afternoon driven convection and decrease the chance of an \nMCS riding the ridge out of the great lakes. The low shear \nenvironment should limit the amount of storms that become severe \nduring the afternoon but given the temps and dewpoints there will be \nplenty of instability to work with.",
